# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Without this file, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` holds CRLF
# while every generator in `tools/scripts/` writes LF. The result is that
# `graph:map:check`, `graph:signatures:check` and the API doc checks all report
# a file as stale when its content is byte-identical -- a false positive that
# appears only on Windows and never in CI.
#
# That is worse than noise. It makes a genuine staleness indistinguishable from
# a phantom one, so the habit becomes ignoring the check, which is how real
# drift reached `master` more than once.
#
# `eol=lf` on the working tree (not merely on the index) is what makes a
# generated file compare identically on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows shell scripts are the exception: the interpreters want CRLF, and
# `ia-graft.cmd` is the launcher every agent workflow in this repository runs.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.wasm binary
*.glb binary
*.ktx2 binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
